{"step_index":1111,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-19T19:51:25Z","thinking":"The issue appears to be the low contrast of the \"What-If\" and threshold sliders against the dark background. The existing track color is too dark, making it difficult to discern. A more vibrant, high-contrast color like sky blue is needed for the slider thumb and fill to improve visibility.\n\n\nInvestigating the threshold elements' low visibility across multiple tabs, the goal is enhancing visual prominence with thicker, high-contrast lines and glowing labels. A side-by-side comparison bar chart in the \"What-If\" simulator could provide a clearer visual delta. Streamlit's base slider CSS classes are under examination for customization options.\n\n\nApplying specific CSS selectors to customize the slider's appearance, targeting the track, fill, thumb, and value labels for improved contrast. Examining chart helper functions, the plan is to increase bar thickness, enhance colors, and improve text contrast in the bar charts and financial waterfall visualizations. The goal is to ensure visual clarity and readability.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"replace_file_content","args":{"AllowMultiple":false,"Description":"Enhance visibility of What-If comparison charts, threshold lines, and gauges","EndLine":396,"Instruction":"Make waterfall, margin comparison, gauges, and threshold lines bold, high-contrast, and clearly visible","ReplacementContent":"def financial_waterfall(financials: dict, model_name: str) -> go.Figure:\n    labels  = ['Gross Revenue', 'Scrap Loss', 'Idle Loss', 'Opp. Loss', 'Net Margin']\n    measure = ['absolute', 'relative', 'relative', 'relative', 'total']\n    values  = [\n        financials.get('gross_revenue', 0),\n        -financials.get('scrap_loss', 0),\n        -financials.get('bottleneck_idle_loss', 0),\n        -financials.get('opportunity_loss', 0),\n        financials.get('net_margin', 0),\n    ]\n\n    fig = go.Figure(go.Waterfall(\n        name='', orientation='v',\n        measure=measure, x=labels, y=values,\n        connector=dict(line=dict(color='rgba(56, 189, 248, 0.7)', width=2)),\n        decreasing=dict(marker=dict(color='#f43f5e', line=dict(color='#fda4af', width=1.5))),\n        increasing=dict(marker=dict(color='#10b981', line=dict(color='#6ee7b7', width=1.5))),\n        totals=dict(marker=dict(color='#38bdf8', line=dict(color='#bae6fd', width=1.5))),\n        text=[f'${abs(v):,.0f}' for v in values],\n        textposition='outside',\n        textfont=dict(color='#f8fafc', size=12, family='JetBrains Mono, monospace'),\n    ))\n    fig.update_layout(\n        **_base_layout(\n            title=dict(text=f'{model_name} — Economic Waterfall Telemetry (USD)', font=dict(size=14, color='#f8fafc')),\n            yaxis=dict(title='Financial Impact ($)'),\n            height=360,\n        )\n    )\n    return fig\n\n\ndef margin_comparison_bar(baseline_margin: float, whatif_margin: float, model_name: str = \"Active Model\") -> go.Figure:\n    \"\"\"Renders a high-contrast side-by-side comparison between Baseline and What-If.\"\"\"\n    scenarios = ['Baseline Scenario', 'What-If Optimized']\n    margins = [baseline_margin, whatif_margin]\n    colors = ['#6366f1', '#10b981']\n\n    fig = go.Figure([\n        go.Bar(\n            x=scenarios,\n            y=margins,\n            marker=dict(color=colors, line=dict(color=['#a5b4fc', '#6ee7b7'], width=1.5)),\n            text=[f'${v:,.0f}' for v in margins],\n            textposition='outside',\n            textfont=dict(color='#f8fafc', size=13, family='JetBrains Mono, monospace'),\n            width=[0.45, 0.45],\n        )\n    ])\n    fig.update_layout(\n        **_base_layout(\n            title=dict(text=f'Margin Delta: Baseline vs What-If ({model_name})', font=dict(size=13, color='#f8fafc')),\n            yaxis=dict(title='Operating Margin ($)'),\n            height=260,\n        )\n    )\n    return fig\n\n\n# ── ANN Surrogate & Digital Twin Charts ───────────────────────────────────────\n\ndef ann_prediction_gauge(val: float, title: str, threshold: float = 0.85) -> go.Figure:\n    \"\"\"Renders a high-contrast gauge for ANN predicted station load with visible threshold.\"\"\"\n    pct = val * 100.0 if val <= 1.0 else val\n    thresh_pct = threshold * 100.0 if threshold <= 1.0 else threshold\n    bar_color = '#f43f5e' if pct >= thresh_pct else ('#f59e0b' if pct >= thresh_pct * 0.85 else '#38bdf8')\n\n    fig = go.Figure(go.Indicator(\n        mode=\"gauge+number+delta\",\n        value=pct,\n        number=dict(suffix=\"%\", font=dict(color='#f8fafc', size=26, family='JetBrains Mono, monospace')),\n        delta=dict(reference=thresh_pct, increasing=dict(color='#f43f5e'), decreasing=dict(color='#10b981')),\n        title=dict(text=f\"<b>{title}</b>\", font=dict(color='#f8fafc', size=13, family='Plus Jakarta Sans, sans-serif')),\n        gauge=dict(\n            axis=dict(range=[0, 100], tickwidth=1.5, tickcolor=\"#94a3b8\", tickfont=dict(color=\"#cbd5e1\", size=10)),\n            bar=dict(color=bar_color, thickness=0.45),\n            bgcolor=\"rgba(30, 41, 59, 0.7)\",\n            borderwidth=1.5,\n            bordercolor=\"rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.3)\",\n            steps=[\n                dict(range=[0, thresh_pct * 0.75], color=\"rgba(16, 185, 129, 0.25)\"),\n                dict(range=[thresh_pct * 0.75, thresh_pct], color=\"rgba(245, 158, 11, 0.25)\"),\n                dict(range=[thresh_pct, 100], color=\"rgba(244, 63, 94, 0.35)\"),\n            ],\n            threshold=dict(\n                line=dict(color='#f43f5e', width=4),\n                thickness=0.85,\n                value=thresh_pct\n            )\n        )\n    ))\n    fig.update_layout(\n        paper_bgcolor=_BG,\n        plot_bgcolor=_BG,\n        font=dict(color='#e2e8f0', family='Plus Jakarta Sans, sans-serif'),\n        margin=dict(t=35, b=10, l=20, r=20),\n        height=200\n    )\n    return fig\n\n\ndef ann_sweep_curve(sweep_x: list, sweep_y: list, output_names: list, current_input: float = None, title: str = \"Neural Metamodel Response Curve\") -> go.Figure:\n    \"\"\"Plots multi-output surrogate response curves across parameter sweep with bold threshold.\"\"\"\n    fig = go.Figure()\n    colors = ['#38bdf8', '#10b981', '#a855f7', '#f59e0b', '#eab308']\n\n    import numpy as np\n    y_arr = np.array(sweep_y)\n    if y_arr.ndim == 1:\n        y_arr = y_arr.reshape(-1, 1)\n\n    for i, name in enumerate(output_names):\n        col_color = colors[i % len(colors)]\n        series_y = y_arr[:, i] * 100.0 if np.max(y_arr[:, i]) <= 1.0 else y_arr[:, i]\n        fig.add_trace(go.Scatter(\n            x=sweep_x,\n            y=series_y,\n            mode='lines',\n            name=name,\n            line=dict(color=col_color, width=3),\n            hovertemplate=f\"Input: %{{x:.1f}}<br>{name}: %{{y:.2f}}%<extra></extra>\"\n        ))\n\n    # Bold High-Contrast Threshold line\n    fig.add_hline(\n        y=85.0, line_dash=\"dash\", line_color=\"#f43f5e\", line_width=2.5,\n        annotation_text=\"85% Bottleneck Limit\",\n        annotation_font=dict(color=\"#f43f5e\", size=12, family='JetBrains Mono, monospace'),\n        annotation_bgcolor=\"rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.85)\",\n        annotation_bordercolor=\"#f43f5e\",\n        annotation_borderwidth=1,\n        annotation_position=\"top right\"\n    )\n\n    if current_input is not None:\n        fig.add_vline(\n            x=current_input, line_dash=\"dot\", line_color=\"#ffffff\", line_width=2,\n            annotation_text=f\"Current Input: {current_input:.1f}\",\n            annotation_font=dict(color=\"#38bdf8\", size=11, family='JetBrains Mono, monospace'),\n            annotation_bgcolor=\"rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.85)\",\n            annotation_bordercolor=\"#38bdf8\",\n            annotation_borderwidth=1,\n            annotation_position=\"bottom right\"\n        )\n\n    fig.update_layout(\n        **_base_layout(\n            title=dict(text=title, font=dict(size=14, color='#f8fafc')),\n            xaxis=dict(title='Input Parameter Value'),\n            yaxis=dict(title='Predicted Output / Utilization (%)'),\n            height=340,\n            legend=dict(orientation=\"h\", yanchor=\"bottom\", y=1.02, xanchor=\"right\", x=1)\n        )\n    )\n    return fig","StartLine":250,"TargetContent":"def financial_waterfall(financials: dict, model_name: str) -> go.Figure:\n    labels  = ['Gross Revenue', 'Scrap Loss', 'Idle Loss', 'Opp. Loss', 'Net Margin']\n    measure = ['absolute', 'relative', 'relative', 'relative', 'total']\n    values  = [\n        financials.get('gross_revenue', 0),\n        -financials.get('scrap_loss', 0),\n        -financials.get('bottleneck_idle_loss', 0),\n        -financials.get('opportunity_loss', 0),\n        financials.get('net_margin', 0),\n    ]\n\n    fig = go.Figure(go.Waterfall(\n        name='', orientation='v',\n        measure=measure, x=labels, y=values,\n        connector=dict(line=dict(color='rgba(0, 240, 255, 0.4)', width=1.5)),\n        decreasing=dict(marker=dict(color=_CYBER['red'])),\n        increasing=dict(marker=dict(color=_CYBER['green'])),\n        totals=dict(marker=dict(color=_CYBER['cyan'])),\n        text=[f'${abs(v):,.0f}' for v in values],\n        textposition='outside',\n        textfont=dict(color='#ffffff', size=11),\n    ))\n    fig.update_layout(\n        **_base_layout(\n            title=dict(text=f'{model_name} — Economic Waterfall Telemetry (USD)', font=dict(size=14, color='#f8fafc')),\n            yaxis=dict(title='Financial Impact ($)'),\n            height=360,\n        )\n    )\n    return fig\n\n\ndef margin_comparison_bar(results: dict) -> go.Figure:\n    if not results:\n        return go.Figure()\n\n    models   = list(results.keys())\n    baseline = [r['baseline'].get('net_margin', 0) for r in results.values()]\n    whatif   = [r['whatif'].get('net_margin', 0) for r in results.values()]\n\n    fig = go.Figure([\n        go.Bar(name='Baseline Scenario', x=models, y=baseline,\n               marker=dict(color=_CYBER['blue'], line=dict(color='rgba(255,255,255,0.15)', width=1)),\n               text=[f'${v:,.0f}' for v in baseline], textposition='outside', textfont=dict(color='#ffffff')),\n        go.Bar(name='What-If Optimized',  x=models, y=whatif,\n               marker=dict(color=_CYBER['cyan'], line=dict(color='rgba(255,255,255,0.15)', width=1)),\n               text=[f'${v:,.0f}' for v in whatif],   textposition='outside', textfont=dict(color='#ffffff')),\n    ])\n    fig.update_layout(\n        **_base_layout(\n            barmode='group',\n            title=dict(text='Net Margin Delta — Baseline vs What-If Optimization', font=dict(size=14, color='#f8fafc')),\n            yaxis=dict(title='Net Operating Margin ($)'),\n            height=320,\n        )\n    )\n    return fig\n\n\n# ── ANN Surrogate & Digital Twin Charts ───────────────────────────────────────\n\ndef ann_prediction_gauge(val: float, title: str, threshold: float = 0.85) -> go.Figure:\n    \"\"\"Renders a high-tech cyberpunk gauge for ANN predicted station load.\"\"\"\n    pct = val * 100.0 if val <= 1.0 else val\n    thresh_pct = threshold * 100.0 if threshold <= 1.0 else threshold\n    bar_color = _CYBER['red'] if pct >= thresh_pct else (_CYBER['orange'] if pct >= thresh_pct * 0.85 else _CYBER['cyan'])\n\n    fig = go.Figure(go.Indicator(\n        mode=\"gauge+number+delta\",\n        value=pct,\n        number=dict(suffix=\"%\", font=dict(color='#f8fafc', size=24)),\n        delta=dict(reference=thresh_pct, increasing=dict(color=_CYBER['red']), decreasing=dict(color=_CYBER['green'])),\n        title=dict(text=title, font=dict(color='#cbd5e1', size=13)),\n        gauge=dict(\n            axis=dict(range=[0, 100], tickwidth=1, tickcolor=\"#64748b\", tickfont=dict(color=\"#94a3b8\", size=10)),\n            bar=dict(color=bar_color, thickness=0.35),\n            bgcolor=\"rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.6)\",\n            borderwidth=1,\n            bordercolor=\"rgba(0, 240, 255, 0.2)\",\n            steps=[\n                dict(range=[0, thresh_pct * 0.75], color=\"rgba(5, 223, 157, 0.15)\"),\n                dict(range=[thresh_pct * 0.75, thresh_pct], color=\"rgba(255, 170, 0, 0.15)\"),\n                dict(range=[thresh_pct, 100], color=\"rgba(255, 51, 102, 0.25)\"),\n            ],\n            threshold=dict(\n                line=dict(color=_CYBER['red'], width=3),\n                thickness=0.8,\n                value=thresh_pct\n            )\n        )\n    ))\n    fig.update_layout(\n        paper_bgcolor=_BG,\n        plot_bgcolor=_BG,\n        font=dict(color='#e2e8f0', family='-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \"Segoe UI\", Roboto, monospace'),\n        margin=dict(t=30, b=10, l=20, r=20),\n        height=190\n    )\n    return fig\n\n\ndef ann_sweep_curve(sweep_x: list, sweep_y: list, output_names: list, current_input: float = None, title: str = \"Neural Metamodel Response Curve\") -> go.Figure:\n    \"\"\"Plots multi-output surrogate response curves across parameter sweep.\"\"\"\n    fig = go.Figure()\n    colors = [_CYBER['cyan'], _CYBER['green'], _CYBER['purple'], _CYBER['orange'], _CYBER['yellow']]\n\n    import numpy as np\n    y_arr = np.array(sweep_y)\n    if y_arr.ndim == 1:\n        y_arr = y_arr.reshape(-1, 1)\n\n    for i, name in enumerate(output_names):\n        col_color = colors[i % len(colors)]\n        series_y = y_arr[:, i] * 100.0 if np.max(y_arr[:, i]) <= 1.0 else y_arr[:, i]\n        fig.add_trace(go.Scatter(\n            x=sweep_x,\n            y=series_y,\n            mode='lines',\n            name=name,\n            line=dict(color=col_color, width=2.5),\n            hovertemplate=f\"Input: %{{x:.1f}}<br>{name}: %{{y:.2f}}%<extra></extra>\"\n        ))\n\n    # Threshold line\n    fig.add_hline(\n        y=85.0, line_dash=\"dash\", line_color=_CYBER['red'],\n        annotation_text=\"85% Bottleneck Limit\", annotation_font=dict(color=_CYBER['red'], size=11),\n        annotation_position=\"top right\"\n    )\n\n    if current_input is not None:\n        fig.add_vline(\n            x=current_input, line_dash=\"dot\", line_color=\"#ffffff\",\n            annotation_text=f\"Current: {current_input:.1f}\", annotation_font=dict(color=\"#ffffff\", size=10),\n            annotation_position=\"bottom right\"\n        )\n\n    fig.update_layout(\n        **_base_layout(\n            title=dict(text=title, font=dict(size=14, color='#f8fafc')),\n            xaxis=dict(title='Input Parameter Value'),\n            yaxis=dict(title='Predicted Output / Utilization (%)'),\n            height=340,\n            legend=dict(orientation=\"h\", yanchor=\"bottom\", y=1.02, xanchor=\"right\", x=1)\n        )\n    )\n    return fig","TargetFile":"C:\\Users\\win-10\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\neurax_app\\utils\\chart_helpers.py","toolAction":"Upgrading chart visibility","toolSummary":"Enhance What-If and threshold visibility in chart_helpers.py"}}]}
